---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import RouteCards from '../components/RouteCards.astro'
---

<Base
  title="Routes · Rudrite Kernels"
  description="The four courses as routes across the map: the kernel path down the TPU side, the JAX and PyTorch paths across the top floors, the XLA path through the waist."
>
  <section class="wrap head">
    <p class="mono-label kicker">four courses · one map under all of them</p>
    <h1>Routes</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A course here is a line drawn across the stack, not a separate site. Each one visits its
      floors in a teaching order, carries its own chapters and its own progress, and hands you
      back to the map when it is done. Pick one to start, or open the map and light a route over
      the cells to see where it goes.
    </p>
    <RouteCards />
    <p class="back"><a class="mono-label" href="/">the map, with all four drawn over it →</a></p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .head { padding-block: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.5rem) 3rem; }
  .kicker { display: block; margin-bottom: 1.1rem; color: var(--accent); text-shadow: var(--bloom); }
  h1 { font-family: var(--grot); font-weight: 800; font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.25rem); line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.03em; }
  .lede { margin: 1.25rem 0 2rem; font-size: 1.125rem; max-width: 62ch; color: var(--ink-mute); }
  .back { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .back a { color: var(--accent-deep); text-decoration: none; }
  .back a:hover { color: var(--accent); text-shadow: var(--bloom); }
</style>
